  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "The total number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>-digit numbers, whose greatest common divisor with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>, is ______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "150",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Prime factorisation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>So, for number having G.C.D with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn></math>&nbsp;to be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>, the number should be odd multiple of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;and does not have&nbsp;factor&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>Odd multiple of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;are</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>102</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>106</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>110</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>114</mn><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mn>998</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>225</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>numbers</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>No. of multiples of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;are</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>102</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>114</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>126</mn><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mn>990</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>75</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>numbers</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Which also include&nbsp;multiple of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math></p><p>Hence, Required&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>225</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
